WEBVTT

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:10.349
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. Friday the sixth, and Teams has actually let us all in. Can you hear me over that fan?</v>

00:00:10.869 --> 00:00:17.870
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, just. Whose new car is that in the car park? It's taking up about a bay and a half.</v>

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:23.949
<v Tomasz Nowak>Not mine. Mine's the one worth less than the tyres on it.</v>

00:00:25.079 --> 00:00:32.079
<v Aisha Begum>Never mind the car, the broken coffee machine in the canteen has ruined my morning. Brown water, no actual coffee.</v>

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:35.219
<v Marcus Hale>So it's operating to its usual specification, then.</v>

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:43.079
<v Sarah Okafor>There is birthday cake in the office, if that helps. Not a balanced breakfast, but there you go.</v>

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:45.869
<v Fiona Doyle>Depends how level you cut the slice.</v>

00:00:47.009 --> 00:00:52.609
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before this becomes a catering meeting. Finished bits first, then what's actually on the list.</v>

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:59.329
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yeah so, I tested the air dryer yesterday and it's all fine now.</v>

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:03.619
<v Sarah Okafor>That's complete, then? Nothing carrying over from that?</v>

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:09.250
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Complete, yeah. Just reporting it back, not another job for today.</v>

00:01:11.670 --> 00:01:17.620
<v Fiona Doyle>And I finished the repair on the waste heat boiler last night. That one's done as well.</v>

00:01:18.489 --> 00:01:21.989
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Two things off rather than two things back on.</v>

00:01:22.569 --> 00:01:32.019
<v Fiona Doyle>Also, we were going to replace the belt on the fire panel, but that's been pushed to next month, so ignore it. Not part of today's work.</v>

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:37.700
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right, cancelled out of this list. I wondered why it was still showing.</v>

00:01:38.209 --> 00:01:46.959
<v Marcus Hale>Just an observation from me: saw the pressure on the guard switch on two dip for a few minutes. It came back on its own.</v>

00:01:47.359 --> 00:01:51.560
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorry, you clipped a bit there. Came back without anyone touching it?</v>

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:59.269
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, on its own. Not asking for a job off the back of that, just saying what I saw.</v>

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:02.430
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Observation only.</v>

00:02:03.099 --> 00:02:08.699
<v Aisha Begum>And the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery for the 11kV board. Same blocker as before.</v>

00:02:11.189 --> 00:02:14.689
<v Fiona Doyle>So there's no confirmed delivery to put into the programme.</v>

00:02:16.949 --> 00:02:20.800
<v Aisha Begum>Exactly. Still blocked, not a fresh action for anyone this morning.</v>

00:02:21.289 --> 00:02:25.840
<v Fiona Doyle>Right, I'll do the pre-use checks on the forklifts on Friday. It's urgent.</v>

00:02:27.530 --> 00:02:31.379
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Fi. Friday for the forklifts, and keeping that marked urgent.</v>

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:33.400
<v Fiona Doyle>Yep, I'll take those.</v>

00:02:35.680 --> 00:02:42.680
<v Sarah Okafor>Priya, can you inspect the water booster for leaks by Thursday? That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:49.979
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, I'll inspect the water booster for leaks by Thursday. Understood, that comes first.</v>

00:02:51.889 --> 00:02:54.689
<v Sarah Okafor>It's the leak inspection on that one, specifically.</v>

00:02:56.500 --> 00:03:00.699
<v Priya Raman>Got you. Inspection for leaks, not signing up to a whole rebuild.</v>

00:03:01.349 --> 00:03:06.599
<v Aisha Begum>I'll swap the filter on the booster pump on Friday. No rush on that one.</v>

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:12.360
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheers, Aisha. Booster pump filter on Friday, no rush. Separate from the water booster inspection.</v>

00:03:13.979 --> 00:03:15.180
<v Aisha Begum>Yeah, that's mine.</v>

00:03:17.289 --> 00:03:22.539
<v Marcus Hale>Sorry, were those two being lumped together? I was talking over the end of that.</v>

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:27.330
<v Aisha Begum>No, separate jobs. Filter swap's the no-rush one.</v>

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:35.379
<v Sarah Okafor>And Aisha, can you take vibration readings on the turbine one today at 2pm? That's fairly important.</v>

00:03:37.139 --> 00:03:41.340
<v Aisha Begum>Yep, I'll take vibration readings on the turbine one today at 2pm.</v>

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:47.460
<v Marcus Hale>Heard that one properly. My audio's stopped doing the underwater thing.</v>

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:53.060
<v Aisha Begum>Lucky you. Mine's mostly fan noise and the occasional word.</v>

00:03:54.819 --> 00:03:58.669
<v Sarah Okafor>Well, the important words were fairly important and 2pm. Thanks, Aisha.</v>

00:03:59.379 --> 00:04:03.930
<v Fiona Doyle>I'll write up the near miss at the wrapper on Friday as well.</v>

00:04:04.699 --> 00:04:08.900
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Fiona. That's the write-up. What priority have we got against it?</v>

00:04:09.860 --> 00:04:13.009
<v Fiona Doyle>Normal priority. I'll have the write-up done on Friday.</v>

00:04:13.860 --> 00:04:17.709
<v Tomasz Nowak>That's the write-up rather than a new investigation we're adding, yeah?</v>

00:04:18.810 --> 00:04:22.660
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, just the write-up of the near miss at the wrapper.</v>

00:04:23.569 --> 00:04:29.170
<v Sarah Okafor>PR, can you organise the toolbox talk for the team by Wednesday? Low priority, that one.</v>

00:04:31.029 --> 00:04:35.930
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team by Wednesday. Low priority, understood.</v>

00:04:38.389 --> 00:04:41.540
<v Sarah Okafor>So that doesn't jump ahead of your leak inspection.</v>

00:04:43.779 --> 00:04:47.980
<v Priya Raman>No, I've got the distinction. Production hold first, toolbox talk low priority.</v>

00:04:50.129 --> 00:04:58.180
<v Sarah Okafor>I'll investigate the pressure drop on the water booster myself. That's a whenever you get a chance one, rather than another urgent job.</v>

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:04.509
<v Olumide Adeyemi>And that's separate from looking for leaks? Just so we're not treating them as one action.</v>

00:05:05.509 --> 00:05:09.709
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, separate. I'll take the pressure-drop investigation; no fixed deadline on that.</v>

00:05:11.930 --> 00:05:17.879
<v Fiona Doyle>Got Sarah Okafor against the pressure drop, then, with whenever you get a chance as the priority.</v>

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:19.949
<v Sarah Okafor>That's right.</v>

00:05:20.839 --> 00:05:26.089
<v Sarah Okafor>Tomasz, can you do a site visit at Harbour Road with the contractor next week?</v>

00:05:27.149 --> 00:05:32.050
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, I'll do the site visit at Harbour Road with the contractor next week.</v>

00:05:34.139 --> 00:05:37.290
<v Fiona Doyle>Just next week against that, not a particular day?</v>

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:42.149
<v Sarah Okafor>Correct, next week is what we've got agreed.</v>

00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:45.300
<v Tomasz Nowak>Fine by me. I've got that one.</v>

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:49.720
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Anyone trying to speak while muted? There's usually one.</v>

00:05:50.769 --> 00:05:56.370
<v Olumide Adeyemi>For once, not me. Nothing else from controls; the air dryer was just the completed update.</v>

00:05:58.639 --> 00:06:04.589
<v Aisha Begum>Nothing else here either. The 11kV board is still a blocker, not something we've picked up today.</v>

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:10.420
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep. No extra actions out of the observations or the blocked bit.</v>

00:06:11.889 --> 00:06:14.689
<v Priya Raman>Important question, then. What sort of birthday cake?</v>

00:06:15.170 --> 00:06:18.670
<v Sarah Okafor>Chocolate. And before anyone asks, I haven't measured the slices.</v>

00:06:21.120 --> 00:06:23.569
<v Marcus Hale>No quality control in that office. Shocking.</v>

00:06:24.579 --> 00:06:26.329
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, we're done. Cheers, everyone.</v>
